WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.504
Tax season often starts with a folder of PDFs and a quiet worry.

00:00:07.504 --> 00:00:10.108
Which page did that number come from?

00:00:10.108 --> 00:00:11.375
Is a form missing?

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:15.175
And do you really want to hand all of it to a chatbot?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.225
Every number, traced to its page.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.409
This is taxtrace, running in your browser, on your own Mac.

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:26.243
At the top, what your workspace holds, then your to-do list,

00:00:26.243 --> 00:00:30.715
and the year's tax-saving moves, ranked by the dollars each one saves.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.421
When your preparer sends more documents,

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:38.107
open the Import tab and choose the files.

00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:43.283
taxtrace shows what it makes of each one: its form, its tax year and its owner.

00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.625
A passport, or a copy you already have, is skipped.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.724
One button files the rest.

00:00:50.724 --> 00:00:55.035
The page then lists your documents by folder, sorted by tax year,

00:00:55.035 --> 00:01:00.075
each tagged with the form it holds, and none of them has left your computer.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.709
Then the entry sheet: everything your tax software will ask,

00:01:08.709 --> 00:01:10.105
in the order it asks.

00:01:10.105 --> 00:01:14.161
Each value shows whether it is ready, an estimate or missing,

00:01:14.161 --> 00:01:17.020
and the document and page it was read from.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.607
Switch to estimates and missing, and only the rows that need you are left.

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:26.969
Each section links to the to-do items that mention it,

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.650
so nothing waits unnoticed.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.359
Last, the chat, for questions about tax rules and forms.

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:37.964
Before anything goes to a cloud model,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:42.009
digits become pound signs and names and towns become stars,

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:44.820
and the page shows exactly what was sent.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.661
And a question with an amount in it never leaves your Mac.

00:01:49.661 --> 00:01:52.855
The model here answers it, and the page says why.
